# A bounded long turn

## Section

`ask/3` returns a handle while AI work continues. In mock mode, the provider
holds its answer long enough for one public inspection. The same Agent runs in
live mode, but a real provider may finish before inspection. Change `backend`
to `:live` and set `OPENAI_API_KEY` to explore that path.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

mock =
  if backend == :mock do
    {:ok, pid} =
      Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(
        script: [%{reply: {:wait, :held, {:text, "Finished"}}}],
        observer: self()
      )

    pid
  end

context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define bounded work

```elixir
defmodule Guide.LongTurn do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_long_turn"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("")})

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Answer in one sentence."

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 1
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.long_turn", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Inspect, release, and await

The mock barrier is notebook coordination. It is not an Agent tool or a
production callback. The request handle keeps its identity before and after
the held provider response.

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.LongTurn, id: "guide-long-turn")
{:ok, request} = Guide.LongTurn.ask(server, "Say you finished.", context: context)

pending =
  if mock do
    receive do
      {:mock_llm_waiting, ^mock, :held, _worker} -> :ok
    after
      5_000 -> raise "The mock provider did not reach its barrier"
    end

    {:ok, view} = Jido.AI.Orchestration.snapshot(server, request_id: request.id)
    :ok = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.release(mock, :held)
    view.request.status
  end

{:ok, answer} = Jido.AI.Request.await(request, timeout: 10_000)
%{request_id: request.id, status_during_mock_wait: pending, answer: answer}
```

Mock mode shows `:pending` before release and `"Finished"` after it. The
caller wait does not keep the AgentServer admission Turn open.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [_]} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
end

:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Long-running turns](../v3/10_long_running_turns.md).
